@notice EIP-712 typehash for the per-leg {AsyncLegRefundAttestation}
         — the THIRD structurally-distinct typehash (mint /
         leg-delivery / leg-refund). Signers attest THORChain
         refunded `refundedAmount` of `assetId` for this `legIndex`
         to our multisig. Distinct struct ⇒ distinct digest ⇒ a mint
         or delivery signature can never verify here.

@param initialOwner Owner permitted to add/remove signers and set threshold.
 @param intentQueue_ The IntentQueue this oracle writes into.
 @param initialSigners Initial signer set; deduplicated implicitly via the mapping.
 @param initialThreshold Initial k-of-n threshold; must be ≥ 1 and ≤ initialSigners.length.

@notice Halts new attestations. Existing attestations and queue
         state are unaffected; this is incident-response only, not
         a permanent kill-switch. Owner-only.

@notice Permanently disabled. Renouncing ownership would brick
         signer rotation, threshold tuning, and the pause/unpause
         incident-response paths (S-2 from 2026-05-24 audit pass).
